# Startup time (ms, hyperfine -N via bench/bench.sh, 2026-10-05)

| e (dir) | e (own source, 1.3k lines) | ed V7 1979 | ed V7 1979 (own source) | nano | vi   | ed GNU (own source) | ls  | nvim | nvim (file) | emacs |
|---------|----------------------------|------------|-------------------------|------|------|---------------------|-----|------|-------------|-------|
| 0.22    | 0.50                       | 0.17       | 0.52                    | 0.49 | 0.50 | 0.81                | 2.4 | 14.7 | 108         | 25.2  |

e opens a file in ~0.22ms (its own 1,284-line source: 0.50ms). nvim takes 108ms.
e renders a full interactive directory browser 10x faster than ls prints filenames.
Thompson's ed as it left Bell Labs (V7, 1979; source from ~/inspiration, three one-line patches in
bench.sh, built static like e) starts empty in 0.17ms, the floor on this box, and takes 0.52ms to page
e.c into its temp file: the time e takes to read the same file and paint a screen. The 2025 GNU ed
needs 0.81ms for that file. (ed reads an ASCII copy: V7 rejects any byte with bit 8 set.)
e is faster than Torvalds's uemacs (same micro-emacs heritage): docs/why-faster-than-uemacs.md.
The top bar times every operation, not just startup: the white reading is that keystroke's own
path from bytes-arrived to frame-composed, in ms to 100ns resolution (an arrow key reads 0.0059ms).
It is patched into the same write as the frame, so the measurement costs no extra syscall.

bench/bench.sh

# Finding a file: type in the browser

`e .` (or `e --pick`) opens the directory browser; typing filters it. The filter searches the
whole tree below the folder you are in, not just the folder itself:

    find: report (1 here, 3 below)
      report.txt                     <- this folder, always listed first
      src/report_helper.c            <- deeper hits show the path they came from
      src/deep/report_deep.md
      src/deep/deeper/report_deepest.py

Results are breadth-first, so the folder you are in comes before one level down, before two.
Enter opens whichever hit is selected, at its path. The walk runs once per folder, on the first
key you type, and is capped (16k entries / 250ms) so a huge or slow tree cannot freeze the
editor — a capped result is marked with `+`. Dot-directories (`.git`) are skipped; dotfiles
are not.


# Build & install (self-compiling, requires gcc/clang)

sh e.c              # build
sh e.c install      # build + symlink to ~/.local/bin/e
sh e.c debug        # ASan/UBSan debug build
sh e.c clean        # remove binary

# Use pre-built binary (no compiler needed)

mkdir -p ~/.local/bin && cp ~/projects/e/e ~/.local/bin/ && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/e && grep -q 'export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"' ~/.bashrc || echo 'export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"' >> ~/.bashrc && export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"
